1
00:00:08,940 --> 00:00:14,140
At sunrise Farmer Lee opens the gate,

2
00:00:14,140 --> 00:00:19,140
The cows come strolling out, they never are late.

3
00:00:19,140 --> 00:00:23,840
A low, soft moo rolls over the hay,

4
00:00:23,840 --> 00:00:28,400
The calves answer back as they wander away.

5
00:00:28,400 --> 00:00:32,560
Down by the red barn, up by the hill,

6
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:38,460
Every friend has a sound of its own to spill.

7
00:00:38,460 --> 00:00:40,960
Come sing along, sing along,

8
00:00:40,960 --> 00:00:43,860
As the morning birds play, morning birds play,

9
00:00:44,040 --> 00:00:48,620
A busy little farm is awake for the day!

10
00:00:49,700 --> 00:00:52,340
The hens scratch circles

11
00:00:52,340 --> 00:00:54,620
Beside the old shed,

12
00:00:54,620 --> 00:00:57,120
Then shake out their feathers

13
00:00:57,120 --> 00:00:59,540
And peck at their bread.

14
00:00:59,540 --> 00:01:04,320
A cheerful cluck-cluck, a flutter and a hop,

15
00:01:04,320 --> 00:01:09,100
They race to the fence when the grain starts to drop.

16
00:01:09,100 --> 00:01:12,960
Down by the red barn, up by the hill,

17
00:01:12,980 --> 00:01:14,240
Up by the hill,

18
00:01:14,240 --> 00:01:18,800
Every friend has a sound of its own to spill.

19
00:01:18,800 --> 00:01:24,520
Come sing along, come sing along,

20
00:01:24,520 --> 00:01:28,820
A busy little farm is awake for the day!

21
00:01:30,250 --> 00:01:34,980
The sheep cross the pasture in soft woolly rows,

22
00:01:35,070 --> 00:01:40,320
The smallest one follows wherever she goes.

23
00:01:40,320 --> 00:01:44,820
A gentle baa-baa drifts over the ground,

24
00:01:44,820 --> 00:01:49,940
While the lambs skip around without making a sound.

25
00:01:49,940 --> 00:01:54,500
The piglets find puddles beside the grain bin,

26
00:01:54,500 --> 00:01:59,640
They wobble and splash with a grin on each chin.

27
00:01:59,640 --> 00:02:01,920
A happy oink-oink,

28
00:02:01,920 --> 00:02:04,540
Then a shake from their toes,

29
00:02:04,540 --> 00:02:09,360
They trot back for lunch with mud on their nose.

30
00:02:09,660 --> 00:02:13,940
The ducks paddle slowly where cattails lean,

31
00:02:13,940 --> 00:02:18,940
They dip their bright bills in the water so clean.

32
00:02:19,460 --> 00:02:24,000
A quack from the stream and a waggle away,

33
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:28,740
Then home to the pond at the close of the day.

34
00:02:28,740 --> 00:02:32,680
Down by the red barn, up by the hill,

35
00:02:33,940 --> 00:02:38,640
Every friend has a sound of its own to spill.

36
00:02:38,640 --> 00:02:43,300
Cows, hens, sheep and ducks all say,

37
00:02:43,300 --> 00:02:48,640
Goodnight to the farm at the end of the day!
